{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For He is testing, etc.</b> And if you would say: from this it follows that the prophet came only to test us — why should he be put to death if the word of HaShem was in his mouth for testing? And it appears that the statement <b>For He is testing</b> does not come to say that HaShem told the prophet to say these things, but rather it comes to give a reason for the signs that HaShem gave. And He said <b>For He is testing</b>, etc., and accordingly HaShem gave this sign for testing." "<b>Or</b> it is possible that this sign and wonder HaShem did not perform for testing at all, but rather to make known that the signs of the heavens declare the wondrous works of HaShem. And He gave the reason ״For He is testing״ as an answer to what Israel might say: Why did HaShem not remove the sign and the wonder, so that Israel would not be led astray after HaShem? Therefore He said <b>For He is testing</b>, etc. — for this reason He left the world to its accustomed course; but aside from this reason, HaShem would act so that the hands of the wicked would not grow strong, and there would be neither sign nor wonder."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:58.081781324Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}